    "body": "> What I'm talking about is directly opening the file in the application using WebDAV and then save it directly to the server with a PUT request.\r\n\r\nThat would be a feature of the other applications. The browser downloads a file (it downloads all URLs it navigates to), and then hands them to the other application. At that point we're outside the realm of web specifications and the browser, and we're talking about the behavior of other applications, which might have their own specs. If such applications want to use WebDAV to upload changes, they're free to do so, and you'd be best served by filing bugs on those applications.\r\n\r\n> And it is also important that you can choose the application to use with a menu just like in a file explorer.\r\n\r\nUI is not in scope for specs; it's a decision by individual browsers as to what they want to implement.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
