    "updated_at": "2021-03-03T00:57:09Z",
    "body": "Browsers can already pass the URL to other applications. There's just no applications that currently consume such a URL, to my knowledge.\r\n\r\nBrowser already know the content type of the files they download. It's in the Content-Type header.\r\n\r\nYou're not being censored. You're free to continue posting on the closed thread. We're just stating that this is a combination of \"already possible\" and \"out of scope\", so it won't result in any changes to the HTML Standard. Since this issue tracker's open issues list is used to track changes to the HTML Standard, we've closed the issue.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
