    "updated_at": "2024-01-03T09:41:52Z",
    "body": "How does the browser pass a url to an application?\r\n\r\nAny application that uses WebDAV like LibreOffice or any Gnome or KDE application can open a URL and write to it. Check Gnome VFS or KDE Kio slaves. In Windows there is also support for WebDAV although I know it less. \r\n\r\nWell, I'm not being censored :). I'm just being hidden under the rug :). Please, open the issue because this is not \"already possible\" and \"out of scope\".",
