    "created_at": "2021-03-03T01:36:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-03T01:37:23Z",
    "body": "I'm not saying that this is something implemented in browsers today. I'm saying this is something browsers could implement today, if they were interested, without any impact on the HTML spec since the interaction between browsers and other programs is not in the scope of the HTML spec. The HTML spec is not about browser features for dealing with arbitrary files; it's about how the browser renders web pages (text/html, roughly).\r\n\r\nSo if you want this feature,  you should file a bug on browsers asking them to implement it. It's not related to the parts of browsers covered by the HTML spec, but is instead an individual product decision each of them would choose to make.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
