    "created_at": "2021-03-03T02:02:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-03T02:02:09Z",
    "body": "> But the content-type attribute is in the HTML Spec scope. This is only about this simple attribute.\r\n\r\nThe `<a>` element already has a `type` attribute which takes a MIME type for the linked resource. The spec says it's purely advisory, and if the linked resource contains a `Content-Type` header, that should be prioritized, but nothing precludes browsers from using it to choose an application included in the OS to open the file.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
